/** @mainpage Qore git Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section gitintro Git Module Introduction

    The git module provides git repository operations for Qore through
    <a href="https://libgit2.org/">libgit2</a>. The module supports both
    disk-backed and virtual (in-memory) repositories, enabling git operations
    in environments without persistent filesystem access.

    Key capabilities:
    - dual-mode repository in @ref Qore::Git "Qore::Git" — disk-backed or
      fully virtual with an in-memory working tree
    - virtual filesystem API for reading, writing, and managing files without
      touching disk
    - full branch, tag, diff, log, and status support
    - remote operations (fetch, push) with cooperative cancellation
    - generic @c ConnectionProvider and @c DataProvider infrastructure
    - high-level configuration management with observer pattern
    - GitHub and GitLab PR/MR management via REST APIs

    @section gitnavigation Documentation

    - @subpage gitgettingstarted -- quick-start examples for disk and virtual repos
    - @subpage gitcookbook -- complete code examples for common scenarios
    - @subpage gitreleasenotes -- version history

    @section gitusermodules User Modules

    - \c GitDataProvider -- @c DataProvider API for git repository operations;
      provides read-file, write-file, list-files, commit, log, and status actions
    - \c GitConnections -- @c ConnectionProvider helpers registering the
      @c gitlocal and @c gitvirtual connection schemes
    - \c GitConfigManager -- high-level configuration management with
      sync/publish semantics and observer-based change detection via
      @c AbstractWatchDataProviderBase
    - \c GitForgeHelper -- GitHub and GitLab pull request and merge request
      management via REST APIs

    @section gitquicklinks Quick Links

    - @ref Qore::Git::GitRepository "GitRepository class reference"
    - @ref gitcookbook "Code examples"
    - @ref gitreleasenotes "Release notes"
*/
